# Local session transcripts
chats.md

# Stray reference PDFs dropped in the working tree — the repo ships no PDFs, so
# this keeps `git add -A` from sweeping one in.
*.pdf

# Per-machine Claude Code settings (project-level .claude/settings.json is fine).
# The glob matters: the editor writes settings.local.json.tmp.<pid>.<hash>
# alongside it, and those get swept in by `git add -A` otherwise.
.claude/settings.local.json*

# uv lock file — project uses standard pyproject, keep repo tool-agnostic
uv.lock
